<title>UK: FirstBus awarded UK's Great Eastern rail-PA.</title>
<headline>FirstBus awarded UK's Great Eastern rail-PA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bus and train operator FirstBus Plc has been awarded the franchise contract to run the Great Eastern passenger rail company as part of the privatisation of Britain's railways, the Press Association news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The PA said the sale meant that 15 of the country's 25 train operating companies have now passed into private hands.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for the government's Office of Passenger Rail Franchising (OPRAF) said that a detailed statement of the terms of this franchise contract, including the planned subsidy levels, would be made at 1030 GMT today.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
